      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "CONTEXT",
          "content": "Rheumatoid arthritis (RA) is differentiated as an early morning exacerbation of the core arthritis condition associated with increase in pain and stiffness in joints and necessitate for medication."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "The aim of the present work was to develop and optimise a pH-triggered delayed-release colon-specific aceclofenac microspheres and to accomplish chronotherapy of RA."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "A 3-factor, 3-level Box-Behnken design (BBD) was used to optimise selected variables. Developed formulation was evaluated for in vivo delayed response and anti-arthritis activity in rats."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "The particle size and encapsulation efficacy of these microspheres were 117.36 ± 10.54 µm and 85.06 ± 5.85%, respectively. Optimised formulation was analysed by SEM, DSC, X-RPD and FTIR. The in vivo evaluation revealed delayed anti-inflammatory activity in carrageenan-induced rats and anti-arthritic activity in freund's adjuvant-induced arthritis rats."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "The optimised aceclofenac microspheres formulation is potential for the chronotherapy of early morning symptoms of RA."
        }
      ]},
